  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/16dfa50b-791b-4cf0-9edf-1322678bb32c-image.png\" style=\"width: 347px; height: 269px;\" /><br />Since circle touches the x-axis at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> hence centre can be taken as <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius <math><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Since y-intercept is 8, by applying Pythagorean theorem<br /><math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Hence two circles are possible<br /><math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />Clearly <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></math> satisfies the given equation of circle.",
    "image": null
  },
